WEBVTT

00:00:00.156 --> 00:00:04.600
ADDIE is a practical instructional design framework for moving from a learning need to a

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.595
finished learning experience.

00:00:05.595 --> 00:00:09.755
The name stands for Analyze, Design, Develop, Implement, and Evaluate.

00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:13.500
Those five words describe the major decisions course creators make:

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.760
understand the problem, plan the experience, build the materials, deliver the course,

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.135
and use evidence to improve it.

00:00:18.135 --> 00:00:18.821
For eLearning,

00:00:18.821 --> 00:00:22.940
ADDIE is useful because it keeps the team from jumping straight into screens, tools,

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.470
graphics, or narration before the instructional problem is understood.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:28.790
Many weak courses begin as content dumps.

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:32.290
A policy document, slide deck, or manual is copied into a course shell,

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:35.211
a quiz is added at the end, and the result is called training.

00:00:35.211 --> 00:00:38.220
ADDIE pushes the team to ask what learners need to do differently,

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.432
not only what information they need to receive.

00:00:40.432 --> 00:00:44.680
ADDIE should be treated as a flexible workflow, not a rigid waterfall requirement.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.730
In real projects, analysis can reveal design constraints, design can expose content gaps,

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.430
development can uncover technical issues,

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:54.520
and evaluation can send the team back to revise earlier decisions.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.800
The value of ADDIE is not paperwork.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.160
The value is disciplined thinking at the right moments.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.375
It also helps separate related but different kinds of work.

00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:05.640
Instructional design defines objectives, strategy, practice, and assessment.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.960
Media production creates graphics, audio, video, and documents.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.200
Course authoring assembles the learning experience.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.450
LMS publishing handles delivery and tracking.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:15.765
Evaluation measures quality and impact.

00:01:15.765 --> 00:01:19.100
When those roles are clear, the course becomes easier to build and maintain.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.680
The practical purpose of ADDIE is decision support.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.015
It helps teams avoid tool-first development, vague objectives, decorative interactions,

00:01:26.015 --> 00:01:28.340
and assessments that do not measure the intended outcome.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.210
A structured process creates room for creativity because the team knows what problem the

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:33.360
course is trying to solve.
